      "id": "q4593xw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Discovery of the Cell"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Robert Hooke discovered the cell in 1665 in a slice of cork, while Anton van Leeuwenhoek observed the first living cell in 1674.",
        "Cell Theory was proposed by Schleiden and Schwann (1839) and extended by Rudolf Virchow (1855) with the phrase 'Omnis cellula-e cellula'.",
        "Prokaryotic cells lack a well-defined membrane-bound nucleus, whereas Eukaryotic cells possess a distinct true nucleus and membrane-bound organelles.",
        "Mitochondria are known as the 'powerhouse of the cell' for ATP production, while Lysosomes are termed 'suicidal bags' due to hydrolytic enzymes.",
        "Plant cells contain a rigid cell wall composed of cellulose, plastids, and large central vacuoles, which are absent in animal cells."
      ],
      "id": "1iskx7l"
    },
